From 014d8a662f5eb6c71aff5bc4210aa85f38adf965 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:23:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add country-level best-time pages; fix variant hash and
 content variety
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Country-shaped queries had no page to land on. Search Console showed
"beste reisezeit panama" answered by Panama City Beach in Florida,
"polen beste reisezeit" by Szczecin, "quando andare in lettonia" by a
plain country forecast page, and "beste reisezeit fortaleza" by that
city's July page — a single month answering a whole-year question.

- New /guides/best-time-to-visit/{country} and /{lang}/{bestTime}/{country}
  for 225 countries in 8 languages. Headline figures average the
  destinations travellers actually ask about rather than every town, and
  each page reports its own within-country spread (Japan: Ishigaki 21°C
  vs Sapporo -4°C in January), which is different for every country.
- The hubs link to all 1,822 city best-time pages by name, which is the
  structural fix for month pages outranking them; month pages now also
  link up to the hub.
- pick() mixed the FNV hash before the modulo. FNV-1a's low bit is the
  XOR-parity of the input, so pick(seed+":a",2) and pick(seed+":b",2)
  were perfectly correlated: the three "independent" choices on a city
  page were one coin flip, and 1,800 city pages rendered 2 distinct
  paragraphs instead of 8. Now 48, worst-case repetition 55.6% -> 3.0%.
- Four month-summary openings per language instead of two, one of them
  shaped as a question and its answer to match the queries these pages
  already receive; visible climate-source line on month pages.

No preposition is ever placed in front of a country name: these strings
serve 225 countries and every language inflects differently ("au Japon",
"aux Pays-Bas", "in die Türkei", "w Hiszpanii"), so headings use
apposition and body text refers back to "the country".

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean, next build clean (4,414 pages), on-demand
rendering checked for Panama/Poland/Latvia/Japan in en/de/it/fr.
